summer. 1. St Luke’s, St Martin’s, S. Each of these is often used when the other would be the right one; St Luke’s day is in October (18th), | St Martin’s in November (11th).
===
**summer.** 1. *St Luke's, St Martin's, S.* Each of these is often used when the other would be the right one; St Luke's day is in October (18th), St Martin's in November (11th).
